    "narrative": "The clear cornerstone of today\u2019s lineup is **Corbin Carroll**, who leads the team with a robust 85.94 score. He is the prime offensive engine facing Zach Agnos; the combination of a favorable 5.15 xERA matchup and the high-leverage #2 spot in the order gives him elite upside, particularly given his capacity to steal bases, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 format. Following closely are **James Wood** (62.77) and **Mickey Moniak** (60.60). Despite **James Wood** facing a tough catcher pop-time disadvantage, his leadoff placement drives his value, while **Mickey Moniak** benefits significantly from the SP skill gap against Eduardo Rodriguez, provided he remains in the #2 hole as projected.\n\nThe decision to start **Kyle Karros** (55.22) over other depth pieces was tight, as his score sits on the fringe of our \"Marginal\" threshold. While **Kyle Karros** faces the same SP-favorable conditions as **Mickey Moniak**, his low-order placement limits his run production ceiling. We are currently navigating a thin bench due to injuries to **Jose Caballero** and **Trevor Story**, alongside the absences of **Josh Naylor** and **Brice Turang** due to a scheduled day off. Consequently, our depth\u2014including prospects like **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**, as well as veterans like **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, and **Zach McKinstry**\u2014remains inactive today.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Mickey Moniak** and **Kyle Karros**. If lineups shift significantly, we lose the order-based floor that keeps these projections in the \"Strong\" to \"Marginal\" range. Meanwhile, **Austin Riley** (55.56) is a high-risk play today; while his SP skill matchup is decent, his poor historical BvP against Alcantara (34 PA) and a negative park factor drag down what would otherwise be a higher raw base projection. We are relying on his ability to capitalize on the pitcher's slow delivery to potentially generate a stolen base, though we remain wary of his recent plate performance.",
